            <ArticleTitle>Treatment strategies for coronary lesions in Takayasu arteritis patients - case report and review of the literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1176-80; discussion 1180</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Takayasu arteritis is type of vasculitis that usually affects the aorta and its major branches. While coronary involvement is seen infrequently, treatment strategy is less clear. Here, we report a case of a 45 year-old woman with Takayasu arteritis who underwent a Y-graft coronary bypass surgery four years previously. We present the long-term follow-up this patient, with a literature review. and we discuss treatment strategies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
